{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The sound of the people in its shouting (be-ra'ah).</b> It is written with a <i>heh</i>, for they were shouting before the calf with five (ה) voices, just as they did for the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar made, of which it is written (Daniel 3:7): ״קל קרנא משרוקיתא קתרוס סבכא פסנתרין״. And there is a further implication of the word ברעה, that they were drawing power from the star that is Mars, whose name is ra'ah; therefore he mentioned מחול, which is a musical instrument, corresponding to the star Mars. And therefore Aaron said to him: ״אתה ידעת את העם הזה כי ברע הוא״ — for evil (ra) is drawn from the force called ra'ah." "<b>And behold.</b> Joshua neither went up with Moses to the mountain nor was he with Israel, for the word וישמע means Torah, that is, he was engaged in Torah; rather, he was at the foot of the mountain waiting for Moses until he descended, and there the manna descended for him alone. And so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in Yoma, first chapter of the tractate on Yom Kippur (Psalms 78:25): ״לחם אבירים אכל איש״ — this is Joshua, for whom manna descended corresponding to all Israel. It is written here ״אכל איש״, and it is written there (Numbers 27:18) ״איש אשר רוח בו״ — we infer איש from איש, but we do not infer איש from האיש. And should one say Moses, since it is written (Numbers 12:3) ״והאיש משה ענו״ — there it says האיש, so we do not infer from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The word ברעה (be-ra'ah, 'in its shouting/evil') is read as carrying multiple senses: the definite article heh as the numeral five; the root רעה as the star Mars; and an allusion to מחול as a musical instrument. רעה as the name of Mars follows medieval astrological nomenclature.", 1 "The gemara's argument turns on the difference between איש (without the definite article, used for Joshua) and האיש (with the definite article, used for Moses): the verbal analogy requires the identical form איש."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:26.315918292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}